      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/alexanderwiederin/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/alexanderwiederin/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/alexanderwiederin/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/alexanderwiederin/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/alexanderwiederin/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/alexanderwiederin/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/alexanderwiederin/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/alexanderwiederin/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "Found during #36692: remove test state that is shared and modified across cases.\n\n`tx_mempool_block_doublespend` ran four cases against one chain and mempool, removing each case’s mempool transaction by hand before the next one. Each case is now its own test with a fresh setup that builds the two spends. The first commit also fixes the last case’s comment, which had the mempool and block spends reversed. The checks are unchanged.\n\nThe second commit makes the two spends distinct transactions. Previously they were identical (deterministic signing), so in the last case the mempool transaction was removed because it was mined rather than as a conflict. The rejection cases are unaffected: they fail with `bad-txns-inputs-missingorspent` either way.",
    "labels": [
